# Banter in Wickermoor Village (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is wickermoor): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ wickermoor_village_01_silas_delphine_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:wickermoor_village and not flag.vessla_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Look at the faces carved in that oak, Delphine. Worst poker faces I ever saw.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: The Founder's statue holds a pose, at least. Going on without a nose is bold billing.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The storm's driving the damp down off that estate. Dreadfang mislikes the scent round those roots.
interject name:silas_vane: A town that carves its worries into a tree instead of leaving? The house owns the deed already.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Let them keep their soggy bark. My hem is taking on water, and I won't play an empty square.
endif
-> END

~ wickermoor_green_queen_inn_02_tobin_rook_cordelia
if name:tobin_hayward and name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:wickermoor_green_queen_inn and not flag.vessla_slain
interject name:tobin_hayward: Three paces back from that hearth, Rook. The grease on those counters would catch quicker than clover.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Chimney draws poorly. And nobody's cleared that rumour board in six months.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Ale and tallow smoke, darling. Every pulse in this room is doing something interesting.
interject name:tobin_hayward: They're stewing in their own damp. Half the timber round that stage has rot behind it.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Roof keeps the rain off, and the ledgers are dry. More than we had on the moor.
endif
-> END

~ wickermoor_village_03_silas_cordelia
if name:silas_vane and name:cordelia_skein and at:wickermoor_village and flag.vessla_slain and not flag.act2_done
interject name:silas_vane: Square's gone quiet now the sky's stopped spitting. You can hear the clock tower over the river.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The villagers' heartbeats have slowed by a full third since the clouds broke. I counted.
interject name:silas_vane: You count pulses. I watch folk stepping out without looking up at the roof first.
interject name:cordelia_skein: A resilient little town, Silas. Even if Old Rusty by the pavilion smells of wet iron.
interject name:silas_vane: Give 'em an hour in the dry and someone'll be running three-card monte off the Founder's plinth.
endif
-> END

~ wickermoor_shop_bakery_04_silas_rook
if name:silas_vane and name:rook_coldwake and at:wickermoor_shop_bakery and flag.act2_done >= 2
interject name:silas_vane: Best spot in the hollow, Rook. Warm flour, and nothing on the racks trying to bite me.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Sound brickwork, sacks clear of the damp. The warmth's no friend to my knuckles, mind.
interject name:silas_vane: Forgot you frostbitten lads don't care for a snug oven. I'll shift my censer by the door.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Leave it be, lad. Warm bread beats cellar mould, even if I can't recall the last loaf I ate.
endif
-> END

~ wickermoor_village_05_delphine_rook
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:rook_coldwake and at:wickermoor_village and flag.act2_done >= 5
interject name:delphine_ravelle: The Green Queen's sign swinging in the dark, Rook. The whole square could fit in a hatbox tonight.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Small town. Doesn't take long to learn which roots lift the cobbles and which roofs leak.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness hasn't cracked a joke since the well. I think I'll miss this muddy little stage.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Folk know our names here now. We'll see the shift through properly.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Stop it, darling. You'll make me sound sentimental in front of the turnip over that door.
endif
-> END

~ rk_dovecote_r1_06_lucan_rook
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:rook_coldwake and at:rk_dovecote_r1 and flag.rk_started and not flag.golub_dead
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, Rook, the moor is moving past that window. Barnaby's pressed so tight to my boots I can scarcely step.
interject name:rook_coldwake: A building has no business strolling across the moor. Especially full of undelivered letters.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The cooing up there is deafening. And some magpie's built a nest of stolen ribbon by the seed sacks.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Disorder from cellar to rafters. If that ladder isn't pegged, I'm citing the keeper in person.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Stay close, good boy. It's only the floorboards groaning, not thunder.
endif
-> END

~ fd_festival_07_tobin_delphine
if name:tobin_hayward and name:delphine_ravelle and at:fd_festival and flag.festival_active and not flag.chuckles_dead
interject name:tobin_hayward: That building's packed with hand pies, Delphine. The grease is sweating through the plaster.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Never mind the pastry. Ribbons roof to roof and a clown balloon the size of a cart. Gaudy.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep between me and that bonfire. The dancers are shoving too close, and I'm dry straw.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Take my elbow. I know a rigged house when the music won't stop, and we're not staying for the encore.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Whatever stretched these lanes three times wide needs pulling up by the root.
endif
-> END

~ fd_silent_church_08_tobin_rook
if name:tobin_hayward and name:rook_coldwake and at:fd_silent_church and flag.festival_active and not flag.chuckles_dead
interject name:tobin_hayward: Hear that, Rook? The drums stop right at the threshold, like someone took shears to them.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Good thick stone, Tobin. Tarps on the windows, but the new timber round the altar's laid square.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Fresh pine in the boards. Not a speck of festival smoke in here.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Could do without the marble lad sneering at the door, mind. Twice regulation height.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Let him sneer, so long as he keeps the sparks and the dancers outside.
endif
-> END
